48
00:02:24,565 --> 00:02:27,025
The Iron Condor is made up of two credit spreads.

49
00:02:27,025 --> 00:02:28,633
So it is a call credit spread,

50
00:02:28,633 --> 00:02:32,079
meaning you are shorting a call that is more expensive than the call you're buying.

51
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:38,310
So you are collecting a credit on the call side. And then you are selling a put credit spread.

52
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:43,705
So I'm selling the 4,700 puts because it is more valuable than the 4,685 put.

53
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:45,975
And I'm also collecting a credit on this side.

54
00:02:45,975 --> 00:02:49,530
The combination of those two is what creates an iron condor.

55
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:53,400
So it is two vertical spreads or two credit spreads.

56
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:58,440
Credit spreads are also vertical spreads. They're just the more technical name for what type of vertical spread you're trading.

57
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:01,569
So in case you didn't know what an iron condor is, a

58
00:03:01,569 --> 00:03:05,219
